 internal/triage/loop_test.go        |  10 ++\n internal/triage/run.go              |   2 +\n internal/worker/loop_test.go        |  10 ++\n internal/worker/run.go              |   6 +-\n 32 files changed, 662 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)\n\ndiff --git a/docs/layout.md b/docs/layout.md\nindex 2d652a3..9ae5549 100644\n--- a/docs/layout.md\n+++ b/docs/layout.md\n@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ internal/costs/             the costs Loop: writes each dirty issue's cost table\n internal/scanner/stale/     the stale closer: a plain controller Loop that comments and closes untouched scanner issues\n internal/agentjob/          helpers the agent loops share: untrusted-input snapshot, admission re-check, agent command and executor job builders, handle save, shutdown-aware wait, post-once\n internal/worker/            the worker loop: claim, agent/test/fix steps, diff guard, code-lane push, draft PR, FinishWith\n-internal/servecmd/          `ard serve` and `ard rebuild-state`: dependency wiring (lock, state, effects, pool adoption, controller); registerLoops takes one line per loop\n+internal/servecmd/          `ard serve` and `ard rebuild-state`: dependency wiring (lock, state, effects, pool adoption, controller); registerLoops takes one line per loop; picks the local or Kubernetes executor from `executor:` and sweeps orphan pods at startup\n internal/redact/            log redaction (secrets and host paths), secret scan and 1 MiB cap (leaf library; close-out commits only LogResult.Clean)\n internal/roles/             starter .ard/ tree (config.yaml, role dirs) embedded for ard init (scanners/cve, scanners/docs, scanners/error-codes, scanners/lint, scanners/missing-tests, scanners/trufflehog, scanners/trufflehog-history, triage/lead, triage/engineer, workers/engineer, reviewers/eng-review, reviewers/license-review, reviewers/security-review)\n internal/pool/              slot arbiter for max_pods (stdlib only, no I/O): priority classes, per-issue triage cap\ndiff --git a/docs/proposal.md b/docs/proposal.md\nindex 3583ba0..b1fcbe6 100644\n--- a/docs/proposal.md\n+++ b/docs/proposal.md\n@@ -320,7 +320,9 @@ A worker job is several executor jobs (`<id>`, `<id>t1`, `<id>f1`, ...) under on\n \n Kubernetes-executor details (decided, design revision 3 of [#54](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/54), recorded in [#312](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/312); the work is split across later parts of #54, and #317 splits into the API layer and the executor). There is no job API on `ard serve`. **Pod shape.** `pre` fetches with the token passed through `http.extraheader` from the environment, never argv or `.git/config`; the git dir is on a `ctl` volume the agent does not mount; the role dir comes from `cfg.SHA`, so the k8s executor refuses a config without a SHA; sidecars are at pinned SHAs; the untrusted inputs and the scrub list travel in the per-job Secret, capped at 768 KiB (over the cap is a permanent failure with a named cause); `pre` copies the static `ard` binary. The `agent` container mounts only `work` and `out` and holds only its model credential via `secretKeyRef`: no GitHub token, no key, no Secret volume, no SA token. It tees stdout to `out/stdout`, enforces its own deadline, writes a done marker and reaps orphans as PID 1. `post` has its own pinned image and never runs a binary from a shared volume. It serves one route, `GET /v1/result`, on the pod IP, guarded by a preshared 32-byte `crypto/rand` key unique to the pod, mounted only in `post` and kept in memory by the controller, compared in constant time. It answers 409 until the agent has terminated and the marker exists, builds the tar in Go and never runs git, serves one request at a time, has header and idle timeouts, never logs Authorization, and exits 0 after the controller confirms or at the deadline. The transport is plain HTTP inside the cluster (the owner's choice): the key grants only this job's result, and a NetworkPolicy limits who can connect.\n \n-**Controller.** `Prepare` builds the local workspace. It mints the read token, the key and the per-job Secret (owned by the Pod), and revokes the token (`DELETE /installation/token`) after `pre` terminates; tokens join the redaction set. Completion is decided only from the kubelet (`containerStatuses`, the agent's `state.terminated`), never from the agent-writable done marker. The controller then pulls the result and safe-untars it into `<id>.result`: it uses `os.Root`; accepts regular files, directories and symlinks, symlinks last; masks modes to 0644/0755; rejects hardlinks, devices, FIFOs, `..`, absolute paths, NUL, duplicates, any `.git` component and case-fold collisions; and caps compressed and decompressed bytes (counted on the stream), entry count, per-file size and gzip ratio. Close-out runs unchanged (`gitx.Snapshot` against `BaseSHA`). The exit code comes from the kubelet only and is saved in `<id>.done`; a pod that ends with no valid result is `Gone`, never `Exited` 0. Statuses: `Running`, `Orphaned`, `Exited`, `TimedOut`, `Gone`. The executor requires GitHub App auth, because a PAT cannot be scoped down. Keys are not persisted: after a restart the Reaper kills orphan pods, and a sweep by an `ard/repo` hash label finds pods with no state record. Handles of the other executor kind report `Gone`. Pod and job names are the lowercased id as `ard-<id>`, at most 63 characters, so ids over 59 are rejected. The client is a thin REST client over the in-cluster SA token behind an interface with a fake, with no client-go. The executor is not an effect: dry-run runs it as local jobs run today.\n+**Serve wiring ([#318](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/318)).** `executor:` in `.ard/config.yaml` picks the executor at startup and it is fixed for the life of the process: a later config whose `executor` differs is a config error (serve pauses, the status issue says `restart ard serve`). Cluster settings are `ard serve` flags with `ARD_K8S_*` env fallbacks, set by the chart: `--k8s-namespace`, `--k8s-instance`, `--k8s-agent-image`, `--k8s-pod-image` (both images pinned by `@sha256:` digest), `--k8s-git-base` (default `https://github.com`), `--k8s-resources` (`cpu=`, `memory=`, `memory-limit=`, `ephemeral-storage=` for the agent container), `--k8s-pre-budget` (5m) and `--k8s-result-grace` (2m). With `executor: k8s`, startup fails (exit 1) if the credential is a personal access token (also under `--dry-run`), a required flag is missing, or the config sets `roles_repo` (not supported with k8s yet). If no config has loaded and the cluster flags are set, the mode is unknown and no job loops are built until restart (`serve.executor_unresolved`). At startup the `pool-adopt` hook calls the executor's `Sweep`, which deletes this repo's job pods and Secrets that no running job record owns; pods with a record go through the Reaper's normal `Orphaned` path. The Reaper maps the executor's end reasons to causes: `evicted` (pod evicted, deleted or never scheduled; transient, one automatic retry), `clone_failed` (transient), and `no_process` for a failed prep step, bad result or missing result. Inputs over the manifest cap close out as `inputs_too_large` and are not retried. Live read tokens are added to the redaction set. `ard config check` prints a note that cluster settings come from `ard serve` flags.\n+\n+**Controller.** `Prepare` builds the local workspace. It mints the read token, the key and the per-job Secret (owned by the Pod), and revokes the token (`DELETE /installation/token`) after `pre` terminates; tokens join the redaction set. Completion is decided only from the kubelet (`containerStatuses`, the agent's `state.terminated`), never from the agent-writable done marker. The controller then pulls the result and safe-untars it into `<id>.result`: it uses `os.Root`; accepts regular files, directories and symlinks, symlinks last; masks modes to 0644/0755; rejects hardlinks, devices, FIFOs, `..`, absolute paths, NUL, duplicates, any `.git` component and case-fold collisions; and caps compressed and decompressed bytes (counted on the stream), entry count, per-file size and gzip ratio. Close-out runs unchanged (`gitx.Snapshot` against `BaseSHA`). The exit code comes from the kubelet only and is saved in `<id>.done`; a pod that ends with no valid result is `Gone`, never `Exited` 0. Statuses: `Running`, `Orphaned`, `Exited`, `TimedOut`, `Gone`. The executor requires GitHub App auth, because a PAT cannot be scoped down. Keys are not persisted: after a restart the Reaper kills orphan pods, and a sweep by an `ard/repo` hash label finds pods with no state record. Handles of the other executor kind report `Gone`. Pod and job names are the lowercased id as `ard-<id>`, at most 63 characters, so ids over 59 are rejected. The client is a thin REST client over the in-cluster SA token behind an interface with a fake, with no client-go. The executor is not an effect: it never calls GitHub to change anything, and dry-run runs it as local jobs run today. The k8s executor mints and revokes read tokens, which are credentials, not effects.\n \n **Layout and limits.** Pod paths are `/job`, `/work`, `/role`, `/sidecar`, `/ard-config`, `/ard-out` and `/ard-bin`; the result roots are `work/` and `out/`, and stdout is `out/stdout`, outside `work/`, so it never shows in `Snapshot.Changed`. Defaults: a 2 GiB `emptyDir` per pod, a result of 512 MiB compressed and 2 GiB unpacked, 200k files, 100 MiB per file, all overridable by `ard serve` flags. **Deadlines.** `h.Deadline = Start + Timeout`; the job-exec deadline is `h.Deadline - min(2m, Timeout/10)`; the pod's `activeDeadlineSeconds` is `Timeout + UploadGrace`, where `UploadGrace` is a 2 minute result-pull grace; the key is revoked at `Deadline` plus that grace; job-exec exits 124 at its deadline, which maps to `TimedOut`. **Settings and images.** Cluster settings (jobs namespace, images, sizes) are `ard serve` flags set by the chart, not `.ard/config.yaml`; `executor` is fixed at startup, and a later config with a different value is a config error until restart. The `ard-agent` image will be public under `ghcr.io/albertcbrown/ard` and holds no secrets (an image test checks it). It carries Go, jq, yq, osv-scanner, govulncheck and golangci-lint at the repo's pins but not trufflehog (AGPL). Roles with a `Dockerfile` use it until in-cluster builds exist.\n \ndiff --git a/internal/agentjob/admit_test.go b/internal/agentjob/admit_test.go\nindex 1990399..d08e39e 100644\n--- a/internal/agentjob/admit_test.go\n+++ b/internal/agentjob/admit_test.go\n@@ -87,6 +87,9 @@ func TestExecJob(t *testing.T) {\n \tif got.ID != \"J\" || got.RoleDir != \"/repo/.ard/reviewers/r\" || got.Dockerfile != \"/repo/.ard/reviewers/r/Dockerfile\" || got.Timeout != 7*time.Minute {\n \t\tt.Errorf(\"job = %+v\", got)\n \t}\n+\tif got.RoleSource.Path != \".ard/reviewers/r\" || got.RoleSource.SHA != cfg.SHA {\n+\t\tt.Errorf(\"role source = %+v\", got.RoleSource)\n+\t}\n \tif got.Sidecar.Name != \"\" {\n \t\tt.Errorf(\"sidecar = %+v\", got.Sidecar)\n \t}\ndiff --git a/internal/agentjob/command.go b/internal/agentjob/command.go\nindex b4efe59..376cc85 100644\n--- a/internal/agentjob/command.go\n+++ b/internal/agentjob/command.go\n@@ -68,6 +68,7 @@ func AgentCommand(reg *agent.Registry, cfg *config.Resolved, role config.Role, s\n // Dockerfile and Sidecar from cfg and Timeout from the role.\n func ExecJob(cfg *config.Resolved, role config.Role, j executor.Job) executor.Job {\n \tj.RoleDir = filepath.Join(cfg.Repo, filepath.FromSlash(role.Dir))\n+\tj.RoleSource = executor.RoleSource{SHA: cfg.SHA, Path: role.Dir}\n \tj.Timeout = role.Timeout\n \tif role.Dockerfile != \"\" {\n \t\tj.Dockerfile = filepath.Join(cfg.Repo, filepath.FromSlash(role.Dockerfile))\ndiff --git a/internal/cli/app.go b/internal/cli/app.go\nindex c4bf5df..9050b87 100644\n--- a/internal/cli/app.go\n+++ b/internal/cli/app.go\n@@ -47,6 +47,22 @@ type Handlers struct {\n type ServeOpts struct {\n \t// Loops names the con